  "interpretation": "Complete means the exact cofactor is 1 after applying every ordered verified refinement overlay. Proven-prime-only requires every stored factor quality to be prime64; probable-prime and other qualities are reported separately. Index shard entries may repeat a factor; repeated entries are counted as storage overhead and reconciled by exact factor value and quality. Distinct index factors absent from all current object factor rows are reported as unused inventory entries. Candidate-population percentages are lower bounds because unindexed candidates have no factorization record. Residual-bit sums overlap in the object hierarchy and are not archive savings; inventory JSON is side information, not a decoder or archive.",
